WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:06.229
They've been properly convinced that there
should be no more superheroes by this four

00:00:06.229 --> 00:00:15.490
panel discussion, and so the Avengers proceed
to commit genocide.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:19.580
I'm here with Tom and Nina and we're going to
talk about our favorite what-ifs.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.320
I just wanted to kind of...

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:25.710
I was looking these issues up and I wanted
to talk about some of the stuff I saw.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:30.420
What's interesting about all of this is that
I noticed in just the quick descriptions of

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:35.370
all the what-ifs, a lot of these what-ifs
have actually come to pass years and years

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:37.210
and years later.

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:39.190
So quickly, I'm just going to run through
them.

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:43.379
What if number one, Spiderman joined the
fantastic four.

00:00:43.379 --> 00:00:44.379
Number two.

00:00:44.379 --> 00:00:45.379
Can you imagine?

00:00:45.379 --> 00:00:47.120
What if Hulk had the brain of Bruce Banner?

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:48.120
What?

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:51.650
Number seven; what if someone else besides
Spiderman had been bitten by a radioactive

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:52.650
spider?

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:53.650
Now quickly, those three...

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:55.100
That would be like 18 different issues.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.129
That'd be great.

00:00:56.129 --> 00:00:57.879
Spiderman did join the Fantastic Four.

00:00:57.879 --> 00:00:59.829
He joined the Future Foundation.

00:00:59.829 --> 00:01:05.267
Hulk has had the brain of Bruce Banner several
times, and most recently in Avengers: Endgame.

00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:08.520
Someone else besides Spiderman had been bitten
by the spider.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:12.930
We've already seen a character named Silk
who was another person who attended the same

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:14.930
science fair as Peter Parker.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:18.750
Now we've got number eight; what if the world
knew that Daredevil is blind?

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:23.620
Famously, in Brian Michael Bendis' Daredevil
run, his identity was revealed to the public.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:27.060
And so everyone knew that Daredevil was blind
lawyer Matt Murdock.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:30.960
Number 10; what if Jane Foster had found the
hammer of Thor?

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:32.040
Coming soon.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.280
Coming soon to a theater near you.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:37.290
Number 30; what if Spiderman's clone had lived?

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:39.810
In the nineties, they did an entire-

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:41.970
That would've sucked, right?

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:46.830
Multi-year run called the Clone Saga, which
is still happening in different ways every

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:47.830
once in a while.

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:50.990
I don't know if it's happening this second,
but I'm pretty sure there's another spider

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:53.200
clone still running around.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:56.150
Number 37; what if Beast and Thing continued
to mutate?

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:59.780
Beast did continue to mutate again, Grant
Morrison's X-Men run.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:01.310
He had another mutation.

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:04.880
Number 44; what if Captain America were revived
today?

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:06.920
That comic book is from the seventies.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:13.500
And since then we've gotten him revived today
in the current crop of Marvel movies.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.240
So anyway, I've talked a lot.

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:18.730
I think I'm going to throw to someone else.

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:20.450
I guess I have the floor.

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:21.450
All right.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:22.450
It's all you, Nina.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:23.450
All right.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:28.480
So my pick is issue number 33, which actually
spins off from a real Iron Man comic and imagines

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:30.370
that the opposite thing happened.

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:34.890
And it is what if Iron Man got trapped in
Camelot?

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:36.900
Yeah.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.840
Based on a multi-arc.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:43.130
So I couldn't find an original copy of Doom
Quest anywhere to read online, which is the

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:49.220
original comic where Doctor Doom and Iron
Man are tussling as they do, and they end

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:55.441
up transported back into Camelot and Iron
Man teams up with King Arthur and Doctor Doom

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:59.780
teams up with Morgan le Fay and they fight
and then...

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:03.590
And Morgan le Fay has been a constant Avengers
bad guy since then.

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:04.590
Yes.

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:07.601
And then basically the two of them put their
differences aside for like five minutes and

00:03:07.601 --> 00:03:12.030
they built a time machine and they leave Camelot.

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:14.690
It does not sound like the-

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:16.130
That's the whole story?

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:17.130
Kind of, yeah.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.390
Morgan le Fay is like, "My half brother, Arthur,
we must defeat him."

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:20.390
Yada-yada.

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:21.390
And so they fight, they fight.

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:24.110
And then the two superheroes are like, "Well
also Camelot sucks.

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:27.540
So let's go back to where we're from."

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:32.350
But what if they imagine that Doctor Doom
betrays Iron Man, and just leaves him in Camelot

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:34.960
forever?

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:37.110
And so he can't build a time machine.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:43.040
He doesn't have any technology, so he just
joins the round table and becomes a knight.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:47.990
And he becomes the successor to King Arthur
and is Sir Anthony, the Man of Iron.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:55.580
And that imagines that Tony Stark was a part
of medieval lore instead of being in present

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:56.580
day.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:57.580
Hello, my liege.

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:03.550
And that is my favorite what-if, because it
is, well, I liked that it took this really

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:09.790
already silly, kind of stupid comic premise
from a real Iron Man series and just went,

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:13.030
but what if Doom was really a jerk and left
him there?

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:14.459
Which he is.

00:04:14.459 --> 00:04:15.740
Yeah.

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:18.660
And just the idea of Tony Stark being like,
"All right, I guess I'm a knight of the round

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:20.310
table now."

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:21.500
I mean, I want to see this.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:24.750
I want them to bring Downey Jr. back for an
exorbitant amount of money and put him in

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:26.540
