They just bust the wall of the Baxter building
and immediately just take out all of the Fantastic

00:12:00.799 --> 00:12:01.799
Four.

00:12:01.799 --> 00:12:06.959
And it should be really exciting except for
they only give this whole 'the Avengers kill

00:12:06.959 --> 00:12:11.110
everyone in the universe', they only give
it two pages.

00:12:11.110 --> 00:12:12.110
Sure.

00:12:12.110 --> 00:12:18.689
Three, if you count the one-page that's dedicated
to the Scarlet Centurion watching them on

00:12:18.689 --> 00:12:24.209
a computer screen, revealing that he's actually
Rama-Tut or Kang the Conqueror.

00:12:24.209 --> 00:12:25.209
What a twist.

00:12:25.209 --> 00:12:26.209
Wow.

00:12:26.209 --> 00:12:31.170
And he disguised himself by putting a hat
over his other hat, which pretty much sums

00:12:31.170 --> 00:12:34.771
up Kang the Conqueror as a character, in my
opinion.

00:12:34.771 --> 00:12:35.771
But I'm a simple man.

00:12:35.771 --> 00:12:39.280
Who could've predicted that this mysterious
person we've never seen before, who would

00:12:39.280 --> 00:12:42.610
tell us to kill all the superheroes, was actually
a villain?

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:44.139
Why did we listen to him?

00:12:44.139 --> 00:12:46.600
He was just so convincing is the thing.

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:49.660
He's compelling and I think that's what...

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:54.150
Okay, so they go out and they knock everybody
out and then Rama-Tut is like, "Hey, just

00:12:54.150 --> 00:12:55.150
kidding.

00:12:55.150 --> 00:12:56.150
Gotcha."

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:57.150
"JK."

00:12:57.150 --> 00:12:58.150
Yeah.

00:12:58.150 --> 00:13:01.670
And then the Avengers split up for a while,
Tony gets drunk and gambles.

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:05.079
Is anyone arrested for a war crime at all?

00:13:05.079 --> 00:13:10.979
No, this is another one of those great Avengers
stories where there's apparently no police

00:13:10.979 --> 00:13:12.360
or United Nations or anything.

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:13.600
Nobody's ever seeing any of this.

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:14.600
Yeah.

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:15.649
No, there's no governing body.

00:13:15.649 --> 00:13:22.050
There's no one to be like, "Wow, these superheroes
just murdered people on an unprecedented scale."

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:25.860
They just sort of started breaking through
buildings and kidnapping people, and then

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:30.540
delivering them to an alien that they met
10 minutes ago.

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:31.540
It's outstanding.

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:35.399
The weirdest part of the whole thing is like,
and it comes out of nowhere, but then a different

00:13:35.399 --> 00:13:40.299
